          %h3#homotopy_groups Homotopy groups
          %p
            The first nontrivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            underlying
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 8
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_8
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_3(E_8) \simeq \mathbb{Z}
          %p as for any compact Lie group. Then the next nontrivial homotopy group is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 15
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_{15}(E_8) \simeq \mathbb{Z}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This means that all the way up to the 15
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coskeleton"} coskeleton
            the group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 8
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_8
            looks,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theoretically
            like the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+space"} Eilenberg-MacLane space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mn 3
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mn 2
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi B
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\mathbb{Z},3) \simeq B^3 \mathbb{Z} \simeq B^2 U(1) \simeq B \mathbb{C}P^\infty
          %h3#Subgroups Subgroups
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exceptional+Lie+group"} exceptional Lie group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E8"} E8
            which corresponds to the
            = succeed "-inclusion" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔰𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 16
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔢
                    %mn 8
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{so}(16) \hookrightarrow \mathfrak{e}_8
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-spin+group"} semi-spin group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SemiSpin%2816%29"} SemiSpin(16)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SemiSpin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 16
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 8
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  SemiSpin(16)
                  \\;\subset\;
                  E_8
          %p
            On the other hand, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+orthogonal+group"} special orthogonal group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 16
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(16)
            is
            %em not
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 8
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_8
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "SemiSpin16#McInnes99a"} McInnes 99a, p. 11
          %p
            Under the inclusion of the maximal compact subgroup, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+representation"} fundamental representation
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mn 8
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 8
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_{8(8)}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branching+rule"} branches
            as
          %svg{:height => "42.41pt", :version => "1.2", :viewbox => "0 0 142.649 42.41", :width => "142.649pt", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", "xmlns:xlink" => "http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"}
