                      %mi ⋯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cdots
          %h2#References References
          %h3#general General
          %p Surveys:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skip+Garibaldi"}> Skip Garibaldi
                ,
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mn 8
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_8
                  , the most exceptional group
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1605.01721"}> arXiv:1605.01721
                )
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/E8_%28mathematics%29"} E₈
          %p
            An introductory survey with an eye towards the relation to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonions"} octonions
            is given in
            %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/octonions/node19.html"} section 4.6
            of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              %em The Octonions
              (
              %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/octonions/octonions.html"}> web
              )
          %h3#HomotopyGroupsReferences Homotopy groups
          %p
            The lower
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 8
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_8
            are a classical result due to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Raoul+Bott"} Raoul Bott
              and H. Samelson,
